  "transcript": [
    {
      "approx_t": 0.0,
      "text": "If you have fair skin, light eyes, and low to medium contrast coloring, you may fall into the light summer color season."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 6.0,
      "text": "So listen closely for your very best colors to wear."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 9.0,
      "text": "Your best neutrals are soft white, dove gray, cool beige, dusty taupe, light mushroom, misty navy, and pale stone."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 17.0,
      "text": "These colors support the skin instead of sitting on top of it."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 19.0,
      "text": "Your best accents are powder blue, periwinkle, cool pink, soft raspberry, lavender, seafoam, icy rose, and muted aqua."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 27.0,
      "text": "These shades bring life into the face without overpowering the eyes."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 30.0,
      "text": "Avoid jet blacks, burnt orange, mustard, deep camel, and neon brights as they create too much visual weight and can make the skin look flat and exhausted."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 39.0,
      "text": "Pause here for the cheat sheet. Comment which celebrity coloration we should cover next."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 43.0,
      "text": "And if you want us to analyze your face, click the link in bio at Qoves.com."
    }
  ],
